# NOTICE

Keylight is a third-party tool. It is not made by, or endorsed by, AJAZZ or
by any other keyboard maker. "AK820" is used only to say which keyboard it
works with.

## Credits

**The keyboard's protocol.** The command numbers, the layout of the board's
configuration space and the way its lighting is stored were worked out from
the EVision V2 driver in
[OpenRGB](https://github.com/OpenRGB/OpenRGB) (the `EvisionV2KeyboardController`
driver, GPL-2.0-or-later), and confirmed against the board itself. No code was
copied from it; what was taken from it are facts about the hardware — which
numbers mean what.

**The key layout.** The places the eighty-two keys sit on the AK820, and what
is written on them, are facts about the keyboard. They were measured once from
a picture of the board and are kept in `ak820-driver/ui/assets/ak820-caps.json`.
The picture itself is not used, and is not in this repository.

**The look.** The app's visual language was modelled on ATK GEAR, the
configuration app that comes with the VXE R1 mouse. That is a look, not a
codebase; nothing was taken from it but measurements.

**The fonts.** Segoe UI Variable, which is on every Windows 11 machine. No
web fonts are downloaded.

## The keyboard's maker

The AK820 is made by 深圳市黑爵同创电子科技有限公司, and sold under the AJAZZ
brand. This project is not connected with either of them.
